---
import Title from "../components/Title.astro"
import Footer from "../components/footer.astro"
import ContactForm from "../components/ContactForm.astro"
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/baseLayout.astro"
import"../styles/global.css"
---
<BaseLayout>
  <main class="content">
    <section class="commission-terms">
      <h1>Eduardo Antonio's Commission Terms of Service</h1>
      <p>contact email: edantoniojuarez@gmail.com</p>
      <p><strong>Effective date: July 22, 2026</strong></p>

      <h2>Summary</h2>

      <ul>
        <li>Personal use is included with standard commissions.</li>
        <li>Commercial use requires a separate commercial license.</li>
        <li>You receive a full-resolution artwork for personal use.</li>
        <li>Personal use includes wallpapers, profile pictures, personal prints, and posting online.</li>
        <li>I retain copyright to the artwork.</li>
        <li>How character design commissions differ from illustration commissions.</li>
        <li>Merchandise, resale, or product use requires additional permission.</li>
        <li>AI training and NFT use are prohibited.</li>
        <li>I may display the artwork in my portfolio or social media unless we have agreed to keep it private.</li>
        <li> Commercial projects require a separate commercial license, which may be
        established through a written contract or written correspondence such as
        email.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        These Terms of Service apply to all commissions unless otherwise agreed upon
        in writing. By commissioning artwork from me, the client acknowledges that
        they have read and agree to these terms.
      </p>

      <h2>1. User Agreement</h2>

      <p>
        By commissioning artwork from me, you confirm that you have read,
        understood, and accepted all terms described within this agreement.
      </p>

      <p>
        I reserve the right to update these terms at any time. The version in effect
        at the time of payment will apply to the current commission.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Copyright</h2>

      <p>
        Unless otherwise agreed upon in writing, I retain full copyright to all
        artwork I create.
      </p>

      <p>
        Commission payment purchases the artwork itself and the usage rights
        outlined below. It does not transfer copyright.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Personal Use License</h2>

      <p>
        Clients may use commissioned artwork for personal, non-commercial purposes,
        including:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>Phone or desktop wallpapers</li>
        <li>Profile pictures and icons</li>
        <li>Printing copies for personal enjoyment</li>
        <li>Posting on social media (credit appreciated whenever practical)</li>
        <li>Sharing with friends and family</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        Clients may not sell, redistribute, or commercially exploit the artwork
        under this license.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Payments</h2>

      <h3>Deposits</h3>

      <p>
        For first-time clients, a 50% non-refundable deposit is required before any
        significant work begins. Work will not begin until the deposit has been
        received.
      </p>

      <p>
        Returning clients may be eligible for different payment arrangements at my
        discretion.
      </p>

      <p>
        <strong>Significant work</strong> means sketching beyond initial concepts,
        line art, rendering, or other substantial progress on the commission.
      </p>

      <h3>Final Payment</h3>

      <p>
        Once the artwork is complete, I will provide a low-resolution, watermarked
        preview for approval.
      </p>

      <p>
        The final high-resolution files will be delivered after the remaining
        balance has been paid in full.
      </p>

      <h3>Payment Plans</h3>

      <p>
        For larger commissions or by request, payment plans may be arranged before
        work begins.
      </p>

      <p>
        Payment plans are considered on a case-by-case basis and may include
        milestone payments throughout the project.
      </p>

      <p>
        Failure to make agreed-upon payments may result in work being paused until
        payment is received.
      </p>

      <h3>Late Payment</h3>

      <p>
        Payment is expected within 14 days of receiving the completed preview or
        milestone unless another arrangement has been agreed upon.
      </p>

      <p>
        If payment is not received within that period, I reserve the right to
        cancel the commission, retain the deposit, and withhold delivery of the
        final files.
      </p>

      <h3>Cancellations</h3>

      <p>
        In the event that I have to cancel your commission due to circumstances
        outside my control, you will receive a full refund.
      </p>

      <p>
        If the client cancels after work has begun, the initial deposit is
        non-refundable as it covers time already reserved and work completed.
      </p>

      <p>
        Depending on the stage of completion, additional refunds may be issued at
        my discretion.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Commercial License</h2>

      <p>
        Commercial use is not included in the standard personal-use license.
        Commercial use requires a separate commercial license agreed upon in writing
        before commercial use begins.
      </p>

      <p>
        A commercial license may cover any commercial use of the commissioned artwork
        or character, including but not limited to:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>Games and interactive media</li>
        <li>Comics, graphic novels, and other published works</li>
        <li>Books and other publications</li>
        <li>Animation and film</li>
        <li>Advertising and promotional materials</li>
        <li>Company branding</li>
        <li>Album covers and other media artwork</li>
        <li>Packaging</li>
        <li>Merchandise and products for sale</li>
        <li>Crowdfunding campaigns and rewards</li>
        <li>Prints, posters, and other products sold to customers</li>
        <li>Other commercial applications agreed upon by both parties</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        Commercial licenses may be limited or broad depending on the project and may
        include restrictions regarding the type of use, duration, territory,
        exclusivity, reproduction, modification, distribution, or other applicable
        rights.
      </p>

      <p>
        Commercial licenses may be structured as a one-time licensing fee, a royalty
        agreement, a combination of both, or another arrangement agreed upon by both
        parties.
      </p>

      <p>
        Unless otherwise agreed upon in writing, a commercial license does not
        transfer copyright ownership. I retain copyright to the artwork.
      </p>

      <p>
        A commercial license may be established through a written contract or through
        written correspondence, including email, that clearly defines the commercial
        rights granted to the client.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Character Design Rights</h2>

      <h3>What Constitutes Character Design</h3>

      <p>
        A character design commission involves substantial creative input from me in
        establishing the character's visual identity and appearance. This may include
        developing the character's silhouette, proportions, facial features,
        hairstyle, clothing, accessories, color palette, visual motifs, and other
        distinguishing features.
      </p>

      <p>
        The client may provide a general concept, personality, setting, themes,
        references, or other creative direction, but the final visual design is
        developed collaboratively with substantial artistic discretion on my part.
      </p>

      <p>
        A commission in which the client has already established a substantially
        complete and specific character design, and I am primarily reproducing or
        illustrating that existing design, is considered an
        <strong> illustration commission</strong> rather than a character design
        commission. Minor modifications to an existing design, such as experimenting
        with clothing, costumes, poses, or accessories, do not by themselves
        constitute character design.
      </p>

      <h3>Personal Character Commissions</h3>

      <p>
        When I create an original character for a client's personal,
        non-commercial use, such as a character for a tabletop roleplaying campaign
        (including Dungeons &amp; Dragons), personal roleplaying, private stories,
        personal artwork, or similar recreational use, the client may freely use and
        develop that character for their own personal purposes.
      </p>

      <p>
        This includes using the character in personal games and campaigns, creating
        additional personal artwork featuring the character, and developing the
        character's personality, backstory, and other personal creative material.
      </p>

      <p>
        I retain copyright to the commissioned artwork and may display the artwork in
        my portfolio, website, social media, and other self-promotion unless
        otherwise agreed upon.
      </p>

      <p>
        Credit as the original character designer is appreciated.
      </p>

      <h3>Commercial Character Projects</h3>

      <p>
        Characters created for commercial projects are subject to the commercial
        licensing terms agreed upon for that project. The client does not
        automatically receive commercial rights, ownership, or the right to exploit
        the character commercially simply because they commissioned the character.
      </p>

      <p>
        A commercial license may grant the client rights to use, reproduce, modify,
        publish, distribute, merchandise, or otherwise commercially exploit the
        character and associated artwork to the extent specifically agreed upon.
      </p>

      <p>
        Depending on the project, commercial character licensing may address character
        ownership, copyright, creator credits, revenue sharing, royalties,
        exclusivity, sublicensing, derivative works, and other applicable rights.
        These terms will be negotiated on a case-by-case basis.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Resale and Redistribution</h2>

      <p>
        Under the standard personal-use license, clients may not:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>Sell the artwork itself</li>
        <li>Redistribute the original files</li>
        <li>Sub-license the artwork or character to others</li>
        <li>Claim authorship of the artwork</li>
        <li>Mint NFTs from the artwork</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        These restrictions do not prevent uses specifically authorized by a separate
        commercial license. Any commercial license may grant additional rights,
        including rights to reproduce, distribute, merchandise, modify, or otherwise
        commercially use the artwork or character, as specifically agreed upon in
        writing.
      </p>

      <h2>8. AI</h2>

      <p>
        My artwork may not be used for AI training, datasets, image generation, or
        machine learning.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Portfolio Rights</h2>

      <p>
        I reserve the right to display commissioned artwork in my portfolio, website,
        and social media unless we have agreed that the commission will remain
        private.
      </p>
          
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
.content {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  min-height: 100%;
  max-height: flex;
}
.commission-terms{
  margin: 5rem
}
main{
  flex: 1;
}
h1{
  font-size: 3rem;
}
h2{
  font-size: 2rem;
}
h3{
  font-size: 1.8rem
}
</style>